<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="70–80 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary and topics · Lesson 13</p>
  <h1>Politics and global issues: <em>map power, evidence, and consequences</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">A public issue involves actors, institutions, rules, resources, values, evidence, and consequences. Neutral language does not require neutrality about every conclusion, and fair framing does not give supported and unsupported claims equal weight. First describe who can decide, who is affected, what the proposal actually does, and what the source establishes. Then evaluate it with explicit criteria.</p>
  <div class="meta-row"><span class="tag">70–80 min core</span><span class="tag">institution → authority → action</span><span class="tag">stakeholder → evidence → effect</span><span class="tag">15–20 min listening and retrieval</span></div>
  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow"><div class="flow-step"><b>Map</b><span>Who decides, implements, and is affected?</span></div><div class="flow-step"><b>Define</b><span>Policy, law, process, and status terms</span></div><div class="flow-step"><b>Evaluate</b><span>Evidence, criteria, distribution, and limits</span></div><div class="flow-step"><b>Respond</b><span>Attribute, challenge, safeguard, and revise</span></div></div>
  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can distinguish government, state, country, nation, legislature, executive, judiciary, local authority, constituent, stakeholder, and civil society without assuming every political system uses the same labels; separate policy, bill, law, legislation, and regulation; use natural collocations for proposing, enacting, implementing, enforcing, amending, repealing, allocating, consulting, advocating, and affecting; distinguish consultation from consent or a vote; evaluate effectiveness, efficiency, feasibility, transparency, accountability, oversight, equality, equity, outputs, outcomes, trade-offs, and unintended consequences; use refugee, asylum-seeker, and internally displaced person accurately and attribute legal classifications; report positions without loaded language or false balance; hear political word-family stress and connected civic chunks; and deliver a neutral evidence-based policy briefing with safeguards and revision conditions.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You recovered attributed reporting, concession, evidence functions, source limits, and a neutral comparison before mapping a public issue.">
    <h3>Reactivate five evidence-and-discourse habits</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Public issue foundation choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="reports">reports</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Nevertheless">Nevertheless</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an interpretation">an interpretation</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a limitation">a limitation</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="whereas">whereas</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="proves">proves</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The article <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="reports" data-hint="Attribute the statement to its source without endorsing it as fact." data-fix="The article reports that the pilot reduced traffic.">choose</button> that the pilot reduced traffic.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Admittedly, the consultation was small. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Nevertheless" data-hint="Introduce a proportionate next step that survives the limitation." data-fix="Nevertheless, it identified access questions worth testing.">choose</button>, it identified access questions worth testing.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>“The lower traffic count may reflect the restriction” is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an interpretation" data-hint="It explains what an observation may mean rather than reporting the number itself." data-fix="The causal explanation is an interpretation.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>A self-selected public survey creates <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a limitation" data-hint="It restricts who the response percentages can represent." data-fix="Self-selection is a limitation on generalization.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The restriction may improve pedestrian safety, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="whereas" data-hint="Compare that intended benefit with a different access concern in a complete clause." data-fix="The restriction may improve pedestrian safety, whereas delivery businesses may face access costs.">choose</button> delivery businesses may face access costs.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice: a policy map comes before a position</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Riverton Central Market access proposal</h3>
    <p><b>Decision and authority:</b> Riverton's elected council may authorize a local traffic trial under the city's charter. Its transportation department would implement signs, permits, and monitoring. The council is not the entire government of a country, and the department does not enact national law.</p>
    <p><b>Proposal:</b> Restrict ordinary private vehicles on four market streets from 10:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. on weekends for three months. Keep access for emergency vehicles and mobility services, and create delivery windows and time-sensitive permits.</p>
    <p><b>Stakeholders:</b> Market visitors, nearby residents, shop owners, employees, delivery drivers, mobility-service users, bus passengers, emergency services, and taxpayers may be affected differently. A stakeholder is not automatically a constituent, decision-maker, supporter, or opponent.</p>
    <p><b>Evidence question:</b> Baseline reports identify safety and air-quality concerns, while consultation responses identify access and business concerns. The consultation was self-selected. It shows what respondents said, not what every resident believes. The proposal is a temporary evidence-building trial, not a permanent ban.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You identified decision authority, implementation, proposal scope, diverse stakeholders, consultation evidence, and temporary evidence-building status without inventing support or opposition.">
    <h3>Discovery check: authority, proposal, actor, and evidence</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Policy discovery choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the elected Riverton council">the elected Riverton council</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the transportation department">the transportation department</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a three-month weekend restriction on four streets">a three-month weekend restriction on four streets</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="people and groups affected in different ways">people and groups affected in different ways</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the views of self-selected respondents">the views of self-selected respondents</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a temporary trial designed to build evidence">a temporary trial designed to build evidence</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a permanent national ban approved by every resident">a permanent national ban approved by every resident</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The source names <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the elected Riverton council" data-hint="Choose the institution the fictional city charter authorizes to approve the local trial." data-fix="The elected Riverton council may authorize the trial.">choose</button> as the decision-maker.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The source names <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the transportation department" data-hint="Choose the administrative body responsible for signs, permits, and monitoring." data-fix="The transportation department would implement the trial.">choose</button> as the implementer.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The actual proposal is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a three-month weekend restriction on four streets" data-hint="Preserve duration, weekend timing, and geographic scope." data-fix="The proposal is a three-month weekend restriction on four market streets.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The stakeholder list contains <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="people and groups affected in different ways" data-hint="Stakeholder status does not reveal a person's opinion or formal authority." data-fix="The stakeholders are people and groups who may be affected differently.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The consultation percentages represent <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the views of self-selected respondents" data-hint="Keep the evidence inside the group that chose to respond." data-fix="The consultation represents its self-selected respondents, not every resident.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The policy status is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a temporary trial designed to build evidence" data-hint="Do not transform the proposed trial into permanent citywide law." data-fix="The proposal is a temporary evidence-building trial.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: identify the institution, actor, and authority</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Useful working meaning</th><th>Precision boundary</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>government</td><td>people and bodies currently exercising public authority</td><td>its structure and scope vary by system</td></tr>
    <tr><td>state</td><td>enduring public institutions and, internationally, a sovereign political entity</td><td>in federal systems, state can also name a subnational unit</td></tr>
    <tr><td>country</td><td>common term for a territory and political community</td><td>useful in general speech but not a substitute for every legal category</td></tr>
    <tr><td>nation</td><td>a community linked by identity, history, culture, or political imagination</td><td>a nation is not always a sovereign state</td></tr>
    <tr><td>legislature</td><td>body that debates and passes proposed legislation as part of lawmaking</td><td>may be called parliament, congress, assembly, or council</td></tr>
    <tr><td>executive</td><td>branch or officials responsible for governing and administration</td><td>relationship to the legislature varies</td></tr>
    <tr><td>judiciary</td><td>courts and judges that interpret and apply law in cases</td><td>organization and powers vary by jurisdiction</td></tr>
    <tr><td>local authority</td><td>institution with powers in a local area</td><td>may be a city, municipality, county, district, or other body</td></tr>
    <tr><td>constituent</td><td>person represented by an elected official in a district or area</td><td>usage may include residents beyond registered voters</td></tr>
    <tr><td>stakeholder</td><td>person or group affected by or able to influence a decision</td><td>does not imply one opinion, right, or degree of power</td></tr>
    <tr><td>civil society</td><td>nongovernmental groups and associations active in public life</td><td>not every nongovernmental organization represents every community</td></tr>
    <tr><td>public consultation</td><td>process for gathering views before or during a decision</td><td>not automatically a referendum, consent process, or representative poll</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <div class="note"><h3>Institution names are system-dependent</h3><p>Do not teach one country's structure as universal. Ask: What does this source call the body? What power does the applicable constitution, charter, or law give it? Is it proposing, authorizing, implementing, reviewing, or deciding a case?</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Stakeholder mapping is not opinion assignment</h3><p>A shop owner may support the trial, oppose it, or hold a mixed view. A resident may also be an employee, mobility-service user, or taxpayer. State the possible interest or effect, then attribute the person's actual position only when a source records it.</p></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You distinguished government, state, legislature, executive, judiciary, local authority, constituent, stakeholder, civil society, and consultation through explicit authority and relationship contexts.">
    <h3>Choose ten institutional and participation terms</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Institution and actor choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="government">government</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="state">state</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="legislature">legislature</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="executive">executive</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="judiciary">judiciary</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="local authority">local authority</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="constituent">constituent</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="stakeholder">stakeholder</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="civil society">civil society</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="public consultation">public consultation</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="universal supporter">universal supporter</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The ministers and departments currently exercising national public authority form the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="government" data-hint="Choose the current governing people and bodies, not the entire country or population." data-fix="The ministers and departments form the government.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The enduring public institutions continue when one administration leaves office; in this contrast they belong to the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="state" data-hint="Distinguish enduring institutions from the current government." data-fix="The enduring institutions belong to the state in this contrast.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The elected assembly debates and passes proposed legislation as its part of lawmaking, so it functions as the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="legislature" data-hint="Choose the lawmaking body, whatever its local name." data-fix="The elected assembly functions as the legislature.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The administration implements authorized programs, so it performs an <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="executive" data-hint="Choose the governing and administrative function rather than judicial review." data-fix="Implementation is an executive function in this system.">choose</button> function.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The independent courts resolve cases and interpret applicable law; collectively they form the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="judiciary" data-hint="Choose the court branch rather than the legislature." data-fix="The courts form the judiciary.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Under the fictional charter, Riverton's council has powers only within the city, so it is a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="local authority" data-hint="Choose an institution whose jurisdiction is a defined local area." data-fix="The Riverton council is a local authority.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>A resident asks the elected representative for District 4 for help. In relation to that representative, the resident is a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="constituent" data-hint="Choose the person represented within the official's district." data-fix="The represented District 4 resident is a constituent.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>A delivery cooperative may be affected by the market decision and can provide evidence, so it is a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="stakeholder" data-hint="The group has a concrete interest but is not necessarily a decision-maker or opponent." data-fix="The delivery cooperative is a stakeholder.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>Independent neighborhood associations and advocacy groups participating in public life are part of <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="civil society" data-hint="Choose public participation outside government institutions." data-fix="The independent associations are part of civil society.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">10</span><span>The city invites written comments and holds a hearing before deciding. This is a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="public consultation" data-hint="The process gathers views but does not itself authorize the policy or represent a binding vote." data-fix="The comment period and hearing form a public consultation.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build policy, law, and civic collocations accurately</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Common actions</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>policy</td><td>planned course of public or organizational action</td><td>propose, adopt, implement, evaluate, revise</td></tr>
    <tr><td>bill</td><td>proposed legislation before enactment</td><td>introduce, debate, amend, pass, reject</td></tr>
    <tr><td>law</td><td>binding legal rule enacted or otherwise recognized in a system</td><td>enact, amend, enforce, comply with, repeal</td></tr>
    <tr><td>legislation</td><td>laws collectively or proposed/enacted legal measures</td><td>introduce, pass, enact, amend, repeal</td></tr>
    <tr><td>regulation</td><td>detailed binding rule made under legal authority</td><td>issue, adopt, enforce, comply with, relax</td></tr>
    <tr><td>program</td><td>organized set of activities or services</td><td>fund, launch, administer, monitor, evaluate</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <div class="note"><h3><span class="ex">Legislation</span> is normally uncountable</h3><p>Use <span class="ex">legislation, a bill, a law, a piece of legislation</span>, or <span class="ex">two legislative measures</span>. In ordinary legal and public-policy English, avoid <span class="cross">a legislation</span> or <span class="cross">two legislations</span> when you mean separate laws.</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Proposal verbs do not promise results</h3><p>A policy may <span class="ex">aim, seek, or be designed to</span> reduce traffic. It does not automatically <span class="ex">ensure, guarantee</span>, or <span class="ex">solve</span> the problem. Report the objective, then evaluate implementation and outcomes.</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Participation verbs have different grammar</h3><p><span class="ex">Advocate for, call for, campaign for or against, lobby officials, lobby for or against, consult residents about</span>, and <span class="ex">protest against</span>. Lobbying means attempting to influence a public decision; the word alone does not establish corruption.</p></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You distinguished policy, bill, law, legislation, regulation, implementation, enforcement, amendment, allocation, advocacy, and direct-object affect patterns.">
    <h3>Complete eleven policy and participation decisions</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Policy and law choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a policy">a policy</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a bill">a bill</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a law">a law</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="legislation">legislation</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a regulation">a regulation</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="implement">implement</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="enforce">enforce</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="amend">amend</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="allocate">allocate</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="called for">called for</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="affected">affected</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a legislation">a legislation</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The council adopts <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a policy" data-hint="Choose a planned course of local action, not automatically a statute." data-fix="The council adopts a policy for the trial.">choose</button> for the temporary trial.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Before enactment, the proposed legal text is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a bill" data-hint="Choose proposed legislation still moving through the applicable process." data-fix="Before enactment, the proposal is a bill.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>After the complete required process and enactment, the measure becomes <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a law" data-hint="Choose the enacted legal rule rather than the earlier bill." data-fix="After enactment, the measure becomes a law.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The assembly passed new housing <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="legislation" data-hint="Use the normally uncountable collective legal noun without an article." data-fix="The assembly passed new housing legislation.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The authorized agency issued <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a regulation" data-hint="Choose one detailed binding rule made under delegated legal authority." data-fix="The agency issued a regulation on permit records.">choose</button> on permit records.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The council authorized the policy; the transportation department will <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="implement" data-hint="Use the verb for putting the authorized plan into operation." data-fix="The department will implement the policy.">choose</button> it.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>Authorized officers <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="enforce" data-hint="Use the verb for making sure the applicable rule is obeyed." data-fix="Authorized officers enforce the traffic rule.">choose</button> the traffic rule.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>To change one section without removing the whole measure, lawmakers may <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="amend" data-hint="Choose the verb for formally changing part of a legal text." data-fix="Lawmakers may amend one section.">choose</button> it.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>The budget will <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="allocate" data-hint="Use the verb for assigning public resources to a stated purpose." data-fix="The budget will allocate $72,000 to monitoring and access safeguards.">choose</button> $72,000 to monitoring and access safeguards.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">10</span><span>Shop-owner representatives <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="called for" data-hint="Use call for before the requested safeguard." data-fix="Shop-owner representatives called for protected delivery windows.">choose</button> protected delivery windows.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">11</span><span>The proposed schedule <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="affected" data-hint="Affect is transitive and takes the group directly, without to." data-fix="The proposed schedule affected weekend delivery drivers.">choose</button> weekend delivery drivers.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Evaluate a proposal without hiding values or inventing legal status</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Criterion</th><th>Question</th><th>Do not confuse it with</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>effectiveness</td><td>Does it achieve the stated objective?</td><td>whether the objective is fair</td></tr>
    <tr><td>efficiency</td><td>What results are achieved with the resources used?</td><td>cheapness alone</td></tr>
    <tr><td>feasibility</td><td>Can it be implemented legally, technically, administratively, and financially?</td><td>whether it should be chosen</td></tr>
    <tr><td>equality</td><td>Are the same rules, access, or resources provided?</td><td>identical outcomes</td></tr>
    <tr><td>equity</td><td>How are barriers, needs, costs, and benefits distributed?</td><td>one automatic policy answer</td></tr>
    <tr><td>transparency</td><td>Can people see the rules, evidence, process, and reasons?</td><td>answerability for results</td></tr>
    <tr><td>accountability</td><td>Who must explain decisions and face review or consequences?</td><td>visibility alone</td></tr>
    <tr><td>oversight</td><td>Who independently or formally monitors conduct and performance?</td><td>the implementer's own publicity</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <div class="note"><h3>Define equality and equity operationally</h3><p>These terms carry value judgments and are used differently across fields. In one access policy, equality might mean the same vehicle rule for everyone, while equity analysis asks whether mobility needs or unequal barriers justify tailored access. State the definition and evidence rather than using either word as a final verdict.</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Outputs, outcomes, impacts, trade-offs, and unintended consequences</h3><p>An <span class="ex">output</span> is an immediate product or service, such as 40 permits issued. An <span class="ex">outcome</span> is a change, such as shorter delivery delays. <span class="ex">Impact</span> often implies a broader or causal effect and needs suitable evidence. A <span class="ex">trade-off</span> is a tension between goals or benefits and costs; do not assume every harm is unavoidable. An <span class="ex">unintended consequence</span> was not the stated objective, but it may be positive or negative.</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Neutral framing is not false balance</h3><p>Attribute positions consistently: <span class="ex">Supporters argue...</span> <span class="ex">Critics question...</span> Then evaluate the evidence for each claim. Avoid loaded labels, but do not call two claims equally supported when the sources differ. Separate factual disagreement, value disagreement, prediction, and legal interpretation.</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Use displacement and protection terms carefully</h3><p>A <span class="ex">refugee</span> is outside their country and meets an applicable international, regional, or national protection definition. An <span class="ex">asylum-seeker</span> is seeking international protection and may be awaiting a final decision. An <span class="ex">internally displaced person</span> was forced or obliged to leave home but has not crossed an internationally recognized state border. <span class="ex">Migrant</span> is not a catchall replacement for people likely to need international protection. Do not assign legal status yourself; attribute it to a competent procedure or reliable source.</p></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You separated transparency, accountability, oversight, effectiveness, efficiency, feasibility, equity, refugee, asylum-seeker, and internal displacement through explicit policy and protection contexts.">
    <h3>Choose ten evaluation and protection terms</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Evaluation and protection choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="transparency">transparency</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="accountability">accountability</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="oversight">oversight</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="effectiveness">effectiveness</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="efficiency">efficiency</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="feasibility">feasibility</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="equity">equity</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="refugee">refugee</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="asylum-seeker">asylum-seeker</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="internally displaced person">internally displaced person</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="automatic legal status">automatic legal status</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Publishing the permit rules, monitoring data, meeting record, and reasons supports <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="transparency" data-hint="Choose visibility of information and process." data-fix="Publishing rules, data, and reasons supports transparency.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Requiring the department to explain missed targets to the council and correct failures creates <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="accountability" data-hint="Choose answerability and a response to performance, not visibility alone." data-fix="Explanation and corrective responsibility create accountability.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>An independent reviewer audits access and safety data, providing <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="oversight" data-hint="Choose formal monitoring by a body outside day-to-day implementation." data-fix="The independent audit provides oversight.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Whether the trial reduces recorded near misses is a question of <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="effectiveness" data-hint="Compare the result with the stated safety objective." data-fix="Achievement of the safety objective concerns effectiveness.">choose</button>.</span></div>
