  <h2>Sound natural: attribute first, then foreground the evidence</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Public discussion becomes easier to follow when the source frame forms a short thought group and the factual or evaluative content carries the final nucleus. Accurate word-family stress matters, but do not make every institutional noun equally prominent. Stress can also mark a correction in authority, scope, or evidence.</p>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Spoken line</th><th>Connection</th><th>Focus</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><b>POL</b>itics · po<b>LIT</b>ical · <b>POL</b>icy</td><td>related public-life terms do not share one stress pattern</td><td>word recognition</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>GOV</b>ern · <b>GOV</b>ernment · govern<b>MEN</b>tal</td><td>unstressed vowels reduce inside the longer forms</td><td>family stress shift</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>LEG</b>islate · legis<b>LA</b>tion</td><td>stress moves toward the suffix in the noun</td><td>law-process family</td></tr>
    <tr><td>According to the CONsultation, / respondents raised ACCESS concerns.</td><td><span class="ex">to</span> may reduce to /tə/ in the source frame</td><td>attributed concern</td></tr>
    <tr><td>The policy protects RIGHTS and duties / while comparing COSTS and benefits.</td><td><span class="ex">and</span> commonly reduces toward /ən/</td><td>paired public values</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <p>Compare <span class="ex">The COUNCIL authorized the trial</span> with <span class="ex">The council authorized a TRIAL, not a permanent ban</span>. Prominence corrects either the actor or the policy scope. A neutral voice does not mean a flat voice; the listener still needs to hear the source, contrast, and conclusion.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read politics-political-policy stress, government-family shift, legislate-legislation shift, reduced according-to attribution, and reduced-and policy-pair listening check" data-success-message="Correct. You recovered public-life stress, two word-family shifts, attributed concern, and paired rights-costs reasoning from five connected U.S. English lines.">
    <h3>Listen for attribution, stress, and scope</h3>
