    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The sensors recorded 31 micrograms per cubic meter, but the file provides no threshold for interpreting that number." data-hint="Report the measurement without inventing a legal or health classification." data-fix="The record gives 31 micrograms per cubic meter and no interpretation threshold."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which air-quality statement stays inside the source?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The sensors recorded 31 micrograms per cubic meter, but the file provides no threshold for interpreting that number.">The sensors recorded 31 micrograms per cubic meter, but the file provides no threshold for interpreting that number.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The number automatically proves a legal violation and a medical diagnosis.">The number automatically proves a legal violation and a medical diagnosis.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="No air measurement was taken during market hours.">No air measurement was taken during market hours.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The 127 supportive responses describe the 184 people who chose to respond, not all Riverton residents." data-hint="Preserve the supportive count and self-selected denominator." data-fix="The support figure applies to the voluntary consultation respondents."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which interpretation of the consultation is accurate?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The 127 supportive responses describe the 184 people who chose to respond, not all Riverton residents.">The 127 supportive responses describe the 184 people who chose to respond, not all Riverton residents.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The consultation proves that every resident supports a permanent ban.">The consultation proves that every resident supports a permanent ban.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Because the survey was voluntary, no respondent expressed any view.">Because the survey was voluntary, no respondent expressed any view.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Thirty-one of the 42 responding shop owners raised concerns about older customers, mobility access, or deliveries." data-hint="Keep the subgroup denominator and the three concern areas." data-fix="Thirty-one of 42 responding shop owners raised access or delivery concerns."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which stakeholder concern is documented?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Thirty-one of the 42 responding shop owners raised concerns about older customers, mobility access, or deliveries.">Thirty-one of the 42 responding shop owners raised concerns about older customers, mobility access, or deliveries.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every shop owner opposed all safety monitoring.">Every shop owner opposed all safety monitoring.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="No business respondent mentioned access.">No business respondent mentioned access.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="A three-month weekend pilot on four streets from 10:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m." data-hint="Preserve duration, days, streets, and daily hours." data-fix="The authorized scope is a three-month weekend pilot on four streets from 10:00 to 4:00."><p class="quiz-question">5. What did the council authorize?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A three-month weekend pilot on four streets from 10:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m.">A three-month weekend pilot on four streets from 10:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A permanent twenty-four-hour citywide vehicle ban.">A permanent twenty-four-hour citywide vehicle ban.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A national law applying to every market.">A national law applying to every market.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Emergency vehicles and registered mobility services are exempt, and deliveries have protected windows plus permits for documented needs." data-hint="Identify both exemptions and the delivery safeguards." data-fix="Emergency and mobility access remain, while delivery windows and permits address documented needs."><p class="quiz-question">6. Which access safeguards are part of the policy?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Emergency vehicles and registered mobility services are exempt, and deliveries have protected windows plus permits for documented needs.">Emergency vehicles and registered mobility services are exempt, and deliveries have protected windows plus permits for documented needs.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="All emergency, mobility, and delivery access is prohibited.">All emergency, mobility, and delivery access is prohibited.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Access depends on an unwritten promise with no process.">Access depends on an unwritten promise with no process.</button></div></div>
