  <h2>Notice and repair the inaccurate public language</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="legislation" data-hint="Legislation is normally uncountable when naming one legal measure." data-fix="The assembly passed a law protecting access to records." data-why="Use a law, a bill, or a piece of legislation for one measure rather than a legislation." data-success-message="Correct. The single enacted measure now uses a countable legal noun."><h3>Repair 1: legal countability</h3><p>Tap the noun phrase with the incorrect article.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="assembly">The assembly passed</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="legislation">a legislation</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="protecting">protecting access to records.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="to" data-hint="Affect takes its object directly." data-fix="The schedule affected weekend delivery drivers." data-why="Affect is transitive in this meaning and does not take to before the affected group." data-success-message="Correct. The verb now connects directly to the affected stakeholder group."><h3>Repair 2: affect pattern</h3><p>Tap the unnecessary preposition.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="schedule">The schedule</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="affected">affected</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="to">to</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="drivers">weekend delivery drivers.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="loaded" data-hint="The description embeds judgments before presenting either position or evidence." data-fix="Supporters described the trial as necessary for safety, while opponents argued that its access costs were too high." data-why="Neutral analysis attributes each evaluation to its source and then examines the evidence instead of using ridiculous and obviously as narrator facts." data-success-message="Correct. The revision attributes both evaluations and leaves their evidence open to analysis."><h3>Repair 3: loaded framing</h3><p>Tap the judgment-loaded frame.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="loaded">The ridiculous opposition rejected the obviously necessary trial</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="meeting">at the meeting.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="status" data-hint="A protection claim is pending, so the report must not announce a final determination." data-fix="Leila has requested international protection and is awaiting a final decision; the report describes her as an asylum-seeker." data-why="A competent procedure or reliable source determines refugee status under the applicable framework. The pending claim supports asylum-seeker here." data-success-message="Correct. The revision describes the pending procedure without inventing its outcome."><h3>Repair 4: invented legal status</h3><p>Tap the unsupported classification.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="request">Leila requested international protection</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="pending">and is awaiting a final decision,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="status">so the report calls her a recognized refugee.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>

  <h2>State the policy relationship before you reveal it</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform><p class="note-line">Respond aloud first. Name the source, actor, authority, action, stakeholder effect, evidence strength, and evaluation criterion. Then reveal and compare.</p><div class="transform-list">
    <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> Attribute the safety case and the shop-owner access concern without choosing a winner.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Supporters argue that the trial may improve safety, while 31 of 42 responding shop owners raised access or delivery concerns.</strong></p></div>
    <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> Distinguish the deciding institution from the implementer.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The council authorized the pilot, and the transportation department will implement it.</strong></p></div>
    <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> State what the voluntary consultation can and cannot represent.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The consultation records the views of 184 voluntary respondents; it does not establish what every resident believes.</strong></p></div>
    <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> Name the access safeguards and their equity purpose without declaring the whole policy equitable.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Mobility exemptions, delivery windows, and documented permits aim to reduce unequal access barriers; the monitoring must show whether they work.</strong></p></div>
    <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> Give the temporary, monitored, revisable recommendation.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Run the temporary independently monitored trial and revise or suspend an access arrangement if evidence shows serious harm.</strong></p></div>
  </div></div>

  <h2>Practice civic discussion without demanding personal disclosure</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>You never need to reveal a real political affiliation, vote, protest history, immigration or protection status, discrimination experience, legal case, benefit claim, income, disability, religion, conflict experience, or opinion about a current government. Use Riverton or a tutor-created public record. The skill is precise civic communication, not testing loyalty or belief.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Authority map:</b> Name one decision-maker, implementer, reviewer, and affected group. Cite the fictional charter, rule, or record that gives each actor a role.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Policy-law switch:</b> Change a policy into a proposed bill, enacted law, or detailed regulation. Replace every action verb and status label that no longer fits.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Stakeholder switch:</b> Give one actor two overlapping roles, such as resident and shop employee. Explain why stakeholder status alone does not predict a position.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Evidence-value switch:</b> Separate a factual disagreement, causal prediction, legal interpretation, and value judgment. State what kind of evidence or authority each would need.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Safeguard switch:</b> Change an access measure, budget, or monitoring result. Reevaluate effectiveness, feasibility, efficiency, equity, and the revision condition.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card"><h3>Final production: deliver a two-minute neutral policy briefing</h3><p>Use Riverton or a new fictional issue. Identify the institution, legal or charter authority, decision-maker, implementer, reviewer, constituents, at least four other stakeholders, policy status, objective, baseline, consultation method, resources, safeguards, outputs, intended outcomes, possible unintended consequence, and revision process.</p><p>Attribute one supporting position and one critical position. Separate the evidence supporting each from the values behind it. Evaluate effectiveness, efficiency, feasibility, transparency, accountability, oversight, equality, and equity without treating a criterion as the verdict. Include one right or obligation only after naming the applicable source or clearly labeling it as a proposal. Use eight policy collocations, three word families with accurate stress, and one source-frame thought group. Your listener changes the authority, evidence, or affected group; revise immediately.</p><p><b>Listener check:</b> Can the listener identify who may decide, who implements, who monitors, who is represented, who is affected, what is policy versus law, what the consultation represents, which claims are factual or evaluative, how costs and benefits are distributed, what protection terms mean, and what evidence would trigger revision?</p></div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You preserved institutional authority, policy status, stakeholder attribution, civic collocations, evaluation criteria, protection terminology, evidence limits, safeguards, and revision conditions."><h3>Seven final decisions</h3><div class="quiz-list">
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The council authorized the trial; the transportation department will implement it; an independent evaluator will provide oversight." data-hint="Keep decision, implementation, and review roles separate." data-fix="The council decides, the department implements, and an independent evaluator monitors."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence maps institutional roles accurately?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The council authorized the trial; the transportation department will implement it; an independent evaluator will provide oversight.">The council authorized the trial; the transportation department will implement it; an independent evaluator will provide oversight.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every stakeholder enacted national law and judged its own case.">Every stakeholder enacted national law and judged its own case.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The consultation itself became the executive, legislature, and judiciary.">The consultation itself became the executive, legislature, and judiciary.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The proposal is a temporary local policy trial, not a permanent national law." data-hint="Preserve duration, level of authority, and legal status." data-fix="The proposal is a temporary local policy trial."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence identifies the policy status correctly?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The proposal is a temporary local policy trial, not a permanent national law.">The proposal is a temporary local policy trial, not a permanent national law.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The three-month pilot is eternal legislation for every country.">The three-month pilot is eternal legislation for every country.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A department implementation plan automatically amends the constitution.">A department implementation plan automatically amends the constitution.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Supporters argue that the measure may improve safety, while responding shop owners raise access and delivery concerns." data-hint="Attribute both positions and avoid loaded narrator judgment." data-fix="Attribute the intended benefit and documented concern to their sources."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which sentence frames competing positions neutrally?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Supporters argue that the measure may improve safety, while responding shop owners raise access and delivery concerns.">Supporters argue that the measure may improve safety, while responding shop owners raise access and delivery concerns.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Only idiots oppose the perfect safety solution.">Only idiots oppose the perfect safety solution.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The evil policy obviously destroys every business.">The evil policy obviously destroys every business.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Transparency publishes the record; accountability requires explanations and correction; oversight independently monitors performance." data-hint="Keep visibility, answerability, and monitoring as three related but different functions." data-fix="Transparency reveals, accountability answers, and oversight monitors."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which sentence distinguishes the three governance criteria?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Transparency publishes the record; accountability requires explanations and correction; oversight independently monitors performance.">Transparency publishes the record; accountability requires explanations and correction; oversight independently monitors performance.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="All three terms mean posting one promotional message.">All three terms mean posting one promotional message.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Oversight means the implementer hides all performance data.">Oversight means the implementer hides all performance data.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The same rule may create different barriers, so an equity analysis examines distribution and safeguards without predetermining the verdict." data-hint="Use equity as a question about distribution, not as an automatic endorsement." data-fix="Equity analysis examines differing barriers and the adequacy of safeguards."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which sentence uses <span class="ex">equity</span> responsibly?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The same rule may create different barriers, so an equity analysis examines distribution and safeguards without predetermining the verdict.">The same rule may create different barriers, so an equity analysis examines distribution and safeguards without predetermining the verdict.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Saying equity automatically proves this exact policy is correct.">Saying equity automatically proves this exact policy is correct.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Equality and equity always require identical outcomes in every context.">Equality and equity always require identical outcomes in every context.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="A person awaiting a final international-protection decision may be described as an asylum-seeker; a competent process or reliable source determines legal status." data-hint="Keep the pending procedure and authority for classification visible." data-fix="Use asylum-seeker for the pending claim and attribute any final legal status."><p class="quiz-question">6. Which sentence handles protection terminology carefully?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A person awaiting a final international-protection decision may be described as an asylum-seeker; a competent process or reliable source determines legal status.">A person awaiting a final international-protection decision may be described as an asylum-seeker; a competent process or reliable source determines legal status.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A language learner can assign refugee status to anyone without evidence or procedure.">A language learner can assign refugee status to anyone without evidence or procedure.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every person who moves is legally identical in every jurisdiction.">Every person who moves is legally identical in every jurisdiction.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Run the temporary independently monitored restriction and revise it if evidence shows serious harm to access or local businesses." data-hint="The B2 listening assessment requires a temporary, monitored, revisable response." data-fix="Run a temporary monitored trial and revise it if evidence shows serious harm."><p class="quiz-question">7. Which recommendation matches the B2 policy-consultation assessment?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Run the temporary independently monitored restriction and revise it if evidence shows serious harm to access or local businesses.">Run the temporary independently monitored restriction and revise it if evidence shows serious harm to access or local businesses.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Introduce a permanent ban immediately and reject all monitoring.">Introduce a permanent ban immediately and reject all monitoring.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Abandon every safety objective before testing any safeguard.">Abandon every safety objective before testing any safeguard.</button></div></div>
  </div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p></div>

  <h2>Reflect: can every public claim identify its authority and evidence?</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card"><h3>Explain the civic architecture</h3><p>Complete these lines aloud: <span class="ex">The institution is...</span> <span class="ex">Its authority comes from...</span> <span class="ex">The actor proposes / authorizes / implements / reviews...</span> <span class="ex">The stakeholder may be affected by...</span> <span class="ex">The consultation represents...</span> <span class="ex">The source supports...</span> <span class="ex">The criterion asks...</span> <span class="ex">The legal or protection term is attributed to...</span> <span class="ex">The safeguard addresses...</span> <span class="ex">Revision occurs if...</span></p><p>Then change the jurisdiction, policy status, consultation method, stakeholder role, or monitoring result. Reformulate every label and conclusion that no longer fits.</p><p><a href="#next-day-retrieval">Return tomorrow for the five-item retrieval check</a> before rereading the lesson.</p></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Next use:</b> Use a fictional or nonpersonal public notice. Write five sentences identifying the institution, actual proposal, affected groups, strongest source-based concern, and one monitorable revision condition.</div>
  <section id="next-day-retrieval" data-lesson-extension="Next-day institution-role, policy-law status, consultation scope, governance criteria, and protection-term retrieval"><h2>Next-day retrieval</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div><p>Return without rereading. Reconstruct authority, policy status, source scope, evaluation function, and careful protection language in five new fictional contexts.</p>
    <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You retained institutional roles, policy-law status, consultation scope, governance criteria, and attributed protection terminology."><h3>Five delayed decisions</h3><div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The assembly passed the bill, the required process enacted it as law, the agency implements it, and the court reviews a disputed interpretation in a case." data-hint="Separate legislative passage, complete enactment, executive implementation, and judicial case review." data-fix="The assembly passes the bill, the complete process enacts the law, the agency implements it, and the court reviews the dispute in a case."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence keeps the institutional functions and legal stages separate?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The assembly passed the bill, the required process enacted it as law, the agency implements it, and the court reviews a disputed interpretation in a case.">The assembly passed the bill, the required process enacted it as law, the agency implements it, and the court reviews a disputed interpretation in a case.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every stakeholder became every branch and decided every function.">Every stakeholder became every branch and decided every function.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The court implemented the bus schedule because consultation enacted it.">The court implemented the bus schedule because consultation enacted it.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The proposed bill may be amended before enactment; if enacted through the required process, it becomes law." data-hint="Preserve proposed status, possible amendment, required process, and enacted status." data-fix="A bill remains proposed legislation until the required enactment process makes it law."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence distinguishes a bill from a law?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The proposed bill may be amended before enactment; if enacted through the required process, it becomes law.">The proposed bill may be amended before enactment; if enacted through the required process, it becomes law.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every policy idea is already a permanent law in every jurisdiction.">Every policy idea is already a permanent law in every jurisdiction.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A legislation is one countable bill after no process.">A legislation is one countable bill after no process.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The voluntary comments reveal what respondents said, but they do not establish the opinion of every resident." data-hint="Keep the evidence inside the self-selected participants." data-fix="Voluntary comments represent respondents, not the whole population."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which sentence reports consultation scope accurately?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The voluntary comments reveal what respondents said, but they do not establish the opinion of every resident.">The voluntary comments reveal what respondents said, but they do not establish the opinion of every resident.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="One voluntary comment proves unanimous consent.">One voluntary comment proves unanimous consent.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A consultation automatically enacts a national referendum result.">A consultation automatically enacts a national referendum result.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Publishing the criteria supports transparency; requiring explanations supports accountability; an independent audit provides oversight." data-hint="Map visibility, answerability, and monitoring to separate mechanisms." data-fix="Transparency publishes, accountability answers, and oversight audits."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which sentence preserves the governance distinctions?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Publishing the criteria supports transparency; requiring explanations supports accountability; an independent audit provides oversight.">Publishing the criteria supports transparency; requiring explanations supports accountability; an independent audit provides oversight.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Transparency, accountability, and oversight all mean hiding the record.">Transparency, accountability, and oversight all mean hiding the record.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A publicity slogan automatically supplies independent oversight.">A publicity slogan automatically supplies independent oversight.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The source describes people forced from home who remain within their country as internally displaced; it does not relabel them refugees without the applicable basis." data-hint="Use the border distinction and attribute any protection classification." data-fix="People forced from home who remain within their country are internally displaced in this source."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which sentence uses displacement terminology carefully?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The source describes people forced from home who remain within their country as internally displaced; it does not relabel them refugees without the applicable basis.">The source describes people forced from home who remain within their country as internally displaced; it does not relabel them refugees without the applicable basis.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every displaced person has crossed an international border and has identical legal status.">Every displaced person has crossed an international border and has identical legal status.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A language exercise can determine legal status without a source or procedure.">A language exercise can determine legal status without a source or procedure.</button></div></div>
